# PUMMELING

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

Pummeling is a partner-based clinch drill designed to develop positional control, underhook acquisition, upper-body coordination and tactile sensitivity during standing grappling exchanges.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-transfer neuromotor and technical exercises for clinch-based combat sports.

---

# Philosophy

Winning the clinch begins long before a throw or takedown.

It begins with position.

Pummeling develops the ability to continuously improve position while maintaining balance, posture and pressure.

CAS selects this exercise whenever clinch efficiency and tactile decision-making are priorities.

